From d643dbf46627a4336289014e33e8a7dc8f13db81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2015 05:51:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] timeserver: Do not synchronise time from any timeserver

OSMC keeps system time with ntpd/systemd-timesyncd and an HTTP Date
header fallback (http-time.service), so ConnMan must not also step or
slew the clock. Return an empty timeserver list unconditionally so
ConnMan never starts its own NTP client, regardless of the TimeUpdates
clock setting, DHCP-provided timeservers or FallbackTimeservers.

Signed-off-by: Sam Nazarko <email@samnazarko.co.uk>
---
 src/timeserver.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/timeserver.c b/src/timeserver.c
index d364f728..25936865 100644
--- a/src/timeserver.c
+++ b/src/timeserver.c
@@ -245,8 +245,7 @@ GSList *__connman_timeserver_get_all(const struct connman_service *service)
 	char **fallback_ts;
 	int index, i;
 
-	if (__connman_clock_timeupdates() == TIME_UPDATES_MANUAL)
-		return NULL;
+	return NULL;
 
 	service_ts_config = connman_service_get_timeservers_config(service);
 
-- 
2.34.1

